/* book Worked example 2: Q: Repeat the image rejection of one Q = 50 tuned circuit at 900 MHz for an IF of 10.7 MHz and of 200 MHz, both high-side. A Hartley receiver with 2 % gain error and 2° phase error follows the 10.7 MHz design. What total image rejection does it reach?
   1. 10.7 MHz IF: fsi = 921.4 MHz; ρ = 921.4/900 − 900/921.4 = 1.02378 − 0.97677 = 0.0470; Qρ = 2.35; α = √(1 + 5.52) = 2.55 = 8.1 dB.
   2. 200 MHz IF: fsi = 1300 MHz; ρ = 1.4444 − 0.6923 = 0.7521; Qρ = 37.6; α = 37.6 = 31.5 dB.
   3. Hartley: ε = 0.02, θ = 2° = 0.0349 rad; ε² + θ² = 0.0004 + 0.00122 = 0.00162; IRR ≈ 4/0.00162 = 2470 = 33.9 dB.
   4. Total for the 10.7 MHz design: 8.1 + 33.9 = 42.0 dB, since the preselector and the image-reject mixer act one after the other.
   Answer: One Q = 50 stage gives 8.1 dB at a 10.7 MHz IF, 19.6 dB at 45 MHz and 31.5 dB at 200 MHz; the 2 %, 2° Hartley mixer adds 33.9 dB, for 42.0 dB in all. */
